#General Question 
Great question!

Is it recommended to run OSDs on MON servers in Ceph?

Best Practice:
It is generally not recommended to run OSDs (Object Storage Daemons) on MON (Monitor) nodes.

Why?
MON nodes are critical for cluster health and quorum. They maintain cluster state and consensus.

Running OSDs on MON nodes can lead to resource contention (CPU, memory, disk I/O), which may affect monitor stability.

Separating MON and OSD roles improves reliability and performance by isolating critical monitor functions.

When is it okay?
In small or test/dev environments, where hardware is limited, it’s sometimes acceptable to co-locate MON and OSD daemons.

For production or larger clusters, best practice is to dedicate separate servers or at least separate disks for MON and OSD roles.

Summary:
Setup	Recommended?
Separate MON and OSD	✅ Best practice
MON + OSD on same node	⚠️ Not recommended (except test/dev)

